1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Thanks for coming on. You've spent fifteen years building things that most people never see.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
That's one way of putting it. Infrastructure is only visible when it breaks.

3
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:45,000
So what actually changed? Honestly, the hardest part was never the technology. It was convincing people to delete things.

4
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:30,000
We had a system nobody understood, and everybody was afraid to touch. So it grew. Fear is a growth strategy for software.

5
00:06:45,000 --> 00:07:05,000
I'd say the single best decision we made was writing down why we did things, not just what we did.

6
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Do I regret it? Some of it. We optimised for a scale that never arrived, and we paid for that every single week.

7
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:22,000
If I could tell my younger self one thing, it would be this: the boring solution is usually the one still running in ten years.
